{"unit":33,"section":2,"cefr":"A1","objective":"form infinitives","skill":"Infinitives 1","heading":"Form infinitives","phrases":[{"he":"להיות או לא להיות, זאת השאלה.","en":"To be or not to be, that is the question.","audio":"https://d1vq87e9lcf771.cloudfront.net/he_v1/cbf8dd666f9d064b8124c54e3ec8af6c","tokens":[{"w":"להיות","h":["to be","be","to become"]},{"w":"או","h":["or"]},{"w":"לא","h":["is not","not","do not"]},{"w":"להיות","h":["to be","be","to become"]},{"w":"זאת","h":["that is (feminine)","that","this is (feminine)"]},{"w":"השאלה","h":["the question"]}]},{"he":"מה אתה רוצֶה לכתוב?","en":"What do you want to write?","audio":"https://d1vq87e9lcf771.cloudfront.net/he_v1/bf048eb818fab4c4aecc864de014e889","tokens":[{"w":"מה","h":["what do","what","what is"]},{"w":"אתה","h":["you","you are"]},{"w":"רוצֶה","h":["want","wants","would like"]},{"w":"לכתוב","h":["to write","writing"]}]},{"he":"אין מה לעשות שם.","en":"There is nothing to do there.","audio":"https://d1vq87e9lcf771.cloudfront.net/he_v1/d0216d9919ceeec13e582d5942740a82","tokens":[{"w":"אין","h":["there is nothing to do","nothing can be done","there is no","not have","not has"]},{"w":"מה","h":["there is nothing to do","nothing can be done","what is","what do","what"]},{"w":"לעשות","h":["there is nothing to do","nothing can be done","to do","do"]},{"w":"שם","h":["there","over there","is putting"]}]},{"he":"אני לא רוצָה למנוע את זה ממנו.","en":"I do not want to deprive him of that.","audio":"https://d1vq87e9lcf771.cloudfront.net/he_v1/b825beba865da628ae56e0d2397d41c2","tokens":[{"w":"אני","h":["I","I am","me"]},{"w":"לא","h":["do not","not","is not"]},{"w":"רוצָה","h":["want","wants"]},{"w":"למנוע","h":["to deprive","to prevent","prevent"]},{"w":"את","h":["it","this","that","you"]},{"w":"זה","h":["it","this","that","it","it is","this"]},{"w":"ממנו","h":["from him","than him"]}]}],"words":[{"he":"להיות","en":"to be","alt":["be","becoming","it's possible","maybe","might","to become"],"from":"lexicon"},{"he":"לעשות","en":"there is nothing to do","alt":["do","nothing can be done","to do"],"from":"lexicon"},{"he":"שם","en":"there","alt":["adjective","is putting","name","noun","over there","puts"],"from":"lexicon"},{"he":"השאלה","en":"the question","alt":[],"from":"lexicon"},{"he":"לכתוב","en":"to write","alt":["writing"],"from":"lexicon"},{"he":"למנוע","en":"to deprive","alt":["prevent","to prevent"],"from":"lexicon"},{"he":"לחזור","en":"return","alt":["come back","to go back","to return"],"from":"skill"},{"he":"לישון","en":"sleep","alt":["sleeping","to sleep"],"from":"skill"},{"he":"לומר","en":"to say","alt":["to tell"],"from":"skill"},{"he":"לבוא","en":"to come","alt":[],"from":"skill"},{"he":"לבקר","en":"to visit","alt":[],"from":"skill"},{"he":"לעזור","en":"help","alt":["helping","to help"],"from":"skill"},{"he":"לראות","en":"see","alt":["seeing","to see"],"from":"skill"},{"he":"לרוץ","en":"run","alt":["running","to run"],"from":"skill"},{"he":"לדעת","en":"to know","alt":[],"from":"skill"},{"he":"או","en":"or","alt":[],"from":"phrase"},{"he":"לא","en":"do not","alt":["is not","not"],"from":"phrase"},{"he":"זאת","en":"that","alt":["that is (feminine)","this is (feminine)"],"from":"phrase"},{"he":"מה","en":"what do","alt":["what","what is"],"from":"phrase"},{"he":"אתה","en":"you","alt":["you are"],"from":"phrase"},{"he":"רוצֶה","en":"want","alt":["wants","would like"],"from":"phrase"},{"he":"אין","en":"there is nothing to do","alt":["nothing can be done","there is no","not have","not has"],"from":"phrase"},{"he":"אני","en":"I","alt":["I am","me"],"from":"phrase"},{"he":"רוצָה","en":"want","alt":["wants"],"from":"phrase"},{"he":"את","en":"that","alt":["it","this","you"],"from":"phrase"},{"he":"זה","en":"that","alt":["it","this","it","it is","this"],"from":"phrase"},{"he":"ממנו","en":"from him","alt":["than him"],"from":"phrase"}],"lexemes":["להיות","לקנות","לחזור","לעשות","לישון","לומר","לדבר","לעבוד","ללכת","לשחות","לבוא","לשחק","לפתוח","לסגור","לבקר","לעזור","לקבל","לבשל","להגיד","לשתות","לגור","למצוא","לראות","לתת","לקחת","לשמוע","לכתוב","לרוץ","לדעת","לגעת","לשים","לשלם","לסבול"],"tips":"Infinitives in Hebrew work in much the same way as in English. The infinitive form of the verb starts with -ל (to). \n\nWe have seen the binyanim pa'al and pi'el so far. This is how both conjugate in the infinitive:\n\n**Pa'al**  \n\nliXXoX  \neg. likhtóv - לכתוב\n\n**Pi'el**\n\nleXaXeX  \neg. leshalém - לשלם\n\nVerbs which end in ה in the singular present, end in ות in the infinitive:\n\n* to swim - liskhót - לשחות  \n* to change - leshanót - לשנות\n\nCertain verbs are irregular in the infinitive. For example, \"to take\" is **לקחת** (lakákhat), and \"to give\" is **לתת** (latét).\n\n**How + infinitive**\n\nYou might come across a sentence where the question word \"how\" is used with an infinitive.\nIt might be translated as \"How to ...\" (e.g. how to do it?), but in some cases the translation could be a bit unnatural.\n\nThis kind of sentence could also be translated as \"How does one...\" / \"How shall/do I/we...\"\n\nFor example (when using the infinitive \"לכתוב\" - to write): \n\n> איך לכתוב את זה? = How does one write this? / How do I write this etc."}